      en: "The Moatize Coal Mine in Tete Province represents one of the largest undeveloped coal reserves on the planet. Spearheaded initially by the Brazilian mining giant Vale, operations began in 2011, fundamentally altering the economic landscape of central Mozambique. The vast open-pit mine extracts high-quality metallurgical coal used for steelmaking, alongside thermal coal. The sheer volume of extraction necessitated the massive reconstruction of the Sena Railway and the creation of the Nacala Logistics Corridor to transport the millions of tons of coal to deep-water ports for Asian markets. Geography K8 — Open-pit mining, fossil fuel extraction, and global commodity markets."
