      en: "The Beluluane Industrial Park (BIP) is Mozambique's premier free-trade zone and industrial hub, located just outside the capital, Maputo. Anchored heavily by the massive Mozal Aluminium Smelter, the park was designed to attract foreign direct investment by offering tax incentives, reliable electricity, and prime access to the Maputo Development Corridor. Today, it hosts dozens of multinational and domestic companies involved in manufacturing, logistics, and heavy industry. BIP serves as a blueprint for industrializing the Mozambican economy, shifting focus from raw resource extraction to value-added manufacturing and regional export. Geography K8 — Special economic zones, industrial parks, and foreign direct investment."
